-- title:
--   Inertia field of a place over p: unramified DVR, residue surjectivity, place descent
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ with $(p:\overline{\mathbb Q})$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), and let $M$ be a non-zero natural number. Write $I_A$ for `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition group of $A$, let $\overline{\mathbb Q}^{I_A}$ be its fixed field, and let $O$ be the preimage of $A$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}^{I_A}$. Four assertions are made. First, $O$ is a discrete valuation ring. Second, its maximal ideal is generated by $p$. Third, the map sending $x\in O$ to the residue class in the residue field of $A$ of the underlying element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is surjective. Fourth, for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — that is, a valuation subring of the field obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M` (the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb Q\ d\ j_q$ for non-zero divisors $d$ of $M$), containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, proper, and a principal ideal ring — if $V$ is fixed by the semilinear action `arithmeticGalois` of every $\sigma\in I_A$, then $V$ is fixed by `arithmeticGalois` $\sigma$ for every $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ fixing $\overline{\mathbb Q}^{I_A}$ pointwise.
--
--   This packages the standard facts that the valuation ring cut out by a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $p$ on the inertia fixed field is an unramified discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$ and with the same (algebraically closed) residue field as the place itself, together with the descent statement that a place of the level-$M$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ fixed by inertia is already fixed by the whole subgroup fixing the inertia field. It serves as the unramified base over which the Deligne–Rapoport model packages at level $M$ are constructed, and is cited by the results producing those packages and identifying their closed points and crossings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_inertiaField_comap_isDVR_and_residue_surjective_and_place_fixed.lean

